  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This was found in the fcrepo4-vagrant setup.  When audit is enable, there will be exceptions in the karaf log for the various indexing routes. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It appears that the baseURL is being set incorrectly for audit objects, so any routes that try to get information regarding those objects throw an exception.  ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I'm not clear on what's causing this, but the baseURL it's complaining about (fedora:info/) seems like it might be coming from the JMS messages that fedora emits for audit....?  ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "org.fcrepo.client.FcrepoOperationFailedException: HTTP operation failed invoking info:fedora/audit/82/ab/0e/cc/82ab0ecc-65a7-4d8b-886c-d6e906e24a28 with statusCode: -1 and message: URI does not specify a valid host name: info:fedora/audit/82/ab/0e/cc/82ab0ecc-65a7-4d8b-886c-d6e906e24a28",
